From 5e0f759cdec8a9c1df0ac51fd850c49d909cd4d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FuJluH <Support@fujluh.ru>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:49:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(desktop): the drawing hands its native objects back

Skia keeps a native object per Paint, Path, Image, Bitmap, Canvas and
Surface until the collector runs, so on Windows an app that draws
constantly pays for them at once in private bytes and only later gives
them back. The hot paths made new ones on every repaint:

- the tray's icon drew a whole surface chain per player state change
  (OctopusArt.icon) and closed nothing of it; the surfaces are closed
  now, and the fifteen window icons are drawn once for the run rather
  than per window shown;
- the taskbar paint, the wash's cover, the shrunken covers and every
  Image, Bitmap, Canvas and Paint in the playlist art store close as
  far as the drawing is through (LateClose where a frame still draws
  with the object, use elsewhere);
- the equalizer's curve made two paths per animated frame and the
  slider and loop paints stayed; they close through LateClose and on
  dispose;
- the lyrics' word mask left its layer open over every frame drawn
  after a throw in the drawing, so each later frame drew into the
  frame before it and the layers piled up. The restore is in a finally.

The playlist art store's byte tally counted every picture added and
none taken away, so it kept telling the cache it was full.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
